[[File:Map-Hispanophone World.svg|thumb|Dark blue = countries where Spanish is the [[language]] of the [[majority]].]]

===Etymology===
{{inh+|en|enm|Spanisch}}, either an alteration of {{m|enm|Spaynisch}} after foreign words for "Spain" or "Spanish" such as {{cog|osp|Espanna}}, {{cog|osp|espannol}} or a {{glossary|partial calque}} of them; equivalent to {{af|en|Spain|-ish}}. 

Sense of "licorice" derives from a local legend in [[Pontefract]], West Yorkshire, where twigs that washed up onto the beaches from the wreckage of a galleon from the Spanish armada were found to be licorice roots.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|spăn'ĭsh}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈspænɪʃ/|a=RP,GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-Spanish.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ænɪʃ|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|Span|ish}}

===Adjective===
